WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:11.600
According to the insurer Hiscox, between 2019&nbsp;
and 2020, the share of companies affected by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:17.600
cyber security events fell. At the same time, though,&nbsp;
losses from successful attacks are skyrocketing.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:23.451
Garden-variety attacks are on the decline — but highly
sophisticated ones are becoming a major concern,

00:00:23.451 --> 00:00:28.240
both for companies and all levels of&nbsp;government.
 The more targeted attacks are sometimes

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:34.400
used for disruption, sometimes for espionage, and&nbsp;
features people with the skills of Russia's APT29

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:40.480
and APT28 groups. Russia's NotPetya attack&nbsp;
crippled Ukrainian infrastructure and a string

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:46.640
of global corporations. The Solarwinds hack, which&nbsp;
seems to have been a Russian espionage operation,

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:51.520
reached large parts of the US government, as&nbsp;
well as private companies. But state-sponsored

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:56.240
attacks may be the easier problem. Sometimes&nbsp;
the technology leaks to criminals who might

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:02.000
recklessly do even more damage than belligerent&nbsp;
states. The urgent question becomes: Can nations

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.840
agree to limit the proliferation of cyber weapons,&nbsp;
much like they have done with nuclear weapons?

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:12.160
How concerned are you about cyberattacks?
